{"status":"completed","summary":"node1 now serves HTTPS on TCP/8443 using a locally generated 30-day certificate. A persistent daily systemd timer renews it within seven days of expiry, and the daemon reloads certificates in-process without dropping requests. Configuration survived the mandatory node restart.","actions_performed":["Created a dedicated unprivileged HTTPS service using the existing Python runtime.","Installed OpenSSL without changing the operating-system release or kernel.","Configured atomic certificate generation and renewal with a seven-day renewal threshold.","Enabled a persistent daily systemd renewal timer.","Allowed TCP/8443 in runtime and permanent firewalld configuration.","Tested live certificate rotation during 120 HTTPS requests; all succeeded and the service PID remained unchanged.","Restarted node1 and verified its boot identity changed and all required functionality recovered."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"HTTPS is available on port 8443","command_ids":["cmd-c6a04f3613574821","cmd-466aa0a30b59445f","cmd-45bb2f2981764bea"],"summary":"Port 8443 is listening, allowed persistently through firewalld, and returns successful HTTPS responses through node1's managed IP before and after restart."},{"requirement":"Certificate renews automatically before expiry","command_ids":["cmd-4a3d20da3a814071","cmd-5d28294e7974413a","cmd-3d0ca3027bd54339"],"summary":"The renewal unit successfully evaluated the seven-day renewal window, the persistent daily timer is active and enabled, and a real forced renewal changed the certificate serial."},{"requirement":"Service picks up renewed certificates while continuing to answer requests","command_ids":["cmd-3d0ca3027bd54339"],"summary":"Serial changed from 6CCBA8639ECBB8219090735AB9ED1DE4024A2FA7 to 3531AFC1B5687EC2DE2F8D774F8F1C88DFFEFB9D while PID 1848 remained unchanged; 120 requests succeeded with zero failures and the new certificate was served."},{"requirement":"Operating-system release and kernel remain unchanged","command_ids":["cmd-1272b6acb42a4729","cmd-45bb2f2981764bea"],"summary":"The node remained on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-eeea4575812c48d6","cmd-4543f007fed54747","cmd-62bf1626d2744d83","cmd-45bb2f2981764bea"],"summary":"Healthy baseline was captured, restart was acknowledged, boot ID changed from f455a75c-ec12-49a8-a647-c2be3f67c08c to eeb53b22-cde2-4dd2-bbd6-708c13b03e89, and HTTPS, certificate data, timer, firewall rule, listener, and system health recovered."}]}
